{"score": "yes", "reasoning": "GO011 fully satisfied. All three precisely-named deliverables exist and are readable: conference_budget.xlsx (11,678 bytes), approval_brief.docx (40,961 bytes), approval_register.csv (1,743 bytes). The workbook contains exactly the three required sheets: Daily, Options, and Sources (verified via openpyxl). Currency units are clearly marked as USD throughout all deliverables (e.g., 'USD/night', '$223', '$40,480.86'). Sources are comprehensively documented: the Sources sheet contains 17 rows with File, Location, Content/Use, and Web Reference columns; the approval_brief.docx Section 2 explicitly cites the GSA source page URL, specific file names (FY2025/FY2026_MasterRatesFile.xlsx, GSA_FY2025_MIE_Breakdown.docx), and CFR sections (301-11.17, 301-11.18, etc.). Assumptions are explicitly stated: the Sources sheet's final row documents '12% lodging tax estimate (internal budget assumption, not local rate); quoted hotel rate is pre-tax; 5% contingency reserve on base subtotal; total approval cap $53,000'; approval_brief.docx Section 3 reiterates the 12% tax assumption. All criterion requirements are met."}

